<title>BELGIUM: Boeing says hopeful of EU deal, despite warning.</title>
<headline>Boeing says hopeful of EU deal, despite warning.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing is still hopeful of reaching an agreement with the European Commission that will allow it to merge with McDonnell Douglas despite tough words from Europe on Tuesday, a top Boeing official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that the proposals put forward (by Boeing) are an honest effort to meet the Commission's concerns. I'm hopeful there will be a deal,&quot; Jim Frank, Boeing's vice president for European affairs, told Reuters.  </p>
<p>Earlier, the European Commission said Boeing, the U.S. planemaker, had not yet met its concerns and said it would block the merger next week unless the concerns were met. - Brussels newsroom: +32 2 287-6800</p>
